# Feature examples

When you add a feature, add a file under `examples/<folder>/` that teaches it.

- One folder per feature. Use a short English name, such as `edit`, `find`, or `jump`.
- Comments at the top say which keys to press and what happens. English only. Short, easy words.
- The rest of the file is text or code to try those keys on.
- Add one line for the new file to `examples/start.txt`.
- Do not put Cargo binaries in `examples/`. A tool goes in `tools/` with a `[[example]]` entry in `Cargo.toml`.
